WEBVTT

00:09.640 --> 00:13.820
You want to know where we're heading?
 Hmm, I'll tell you where.

00:14.070 --> 00:15.710
Wherever the wind takes us.

00:16.650 --> 00:19.130
Wherever the wind takes us!

00:29.720 --> 00:32.900
Well, everybody's got a look-alike, right?

00:44.140 --> 00:50.570
<b>Ranking of Kings</b>

00:44.140 --> 00:50.570
<b>— The Treasure Chest of Courage —</b>

00:53.530 --> 00:58.280
<i>The callous absurdity I've 
carried with me since birth</i>

00:58.280 --> 01:03.950
<i>meant playing shadow tag to find my next meal</i>

01:04.500 --> 01:07.710
<i>Bit by bit, my heart got bent out of shape</i>

01:07.710 --> 01:10.710
<i>until I tuned out both 
the cheers and the jeers</i>

01:12.920 --> 01:17.590
<i>That's how I survived my initial loneliness</i>

01:17.590 --> 01:22.600
<i>Night falls and the darkness grows</i>

01:23.020 --> 01:27.810
<i>blending in, coalescing</i>

01:28.150 --> 01:32.570
<i>around so trivial a fate as my own</i>

01:32.570 --> 01:35.400
<i>Hey, I want to get through to you</i>

01:35.400 --> 01:39.450
<i>though I may only know commonplace words</i>

01:40.950 --> 01:43.740
<i>It's so frustrating having to be like this</i>

01:43.740 --> 01:46.660
<i>Hey, never mind that it may not be easy</i>

01:46.660 --> 01:51.090
<i>to become angry or let yourself cry</i>

01:52.210 --> 01:55.800
<i>because someone could be listening in</i>

01:55.800 --> 01:59.010
<i>The only thing that's 
certain is the temperature</i>

02:01.260 --> 02:06.180
<i>whether or not we can speak heart to heart</i>

02:07.850 --> 02:11.020
<b>Return of the Sword King</b>

02:11.190 --> 02:12.270
Is that it?

02:12.270 --> 02:13.020
Yes.

02:16.120 --> 02:17.940
It looks like it's in ruins.

02:17.940 --> 02:19.370
That's because it is.

02:50.820 --> 02:52.340
This is the treasure vault.

02:52.900 --> 02:55.760
Only those who are chosen 
may proceed any farther.

02:56.200 --> 02:57.160
Wait here.

02:57.160 --> 02:57.760
Yes, sire.

03:13.370 --> 03:15.420
Hmph. Big deal.

03:20.980 --> 03:22.120
What are these?

03:22.120 --> 03:24.480
You have a keen eye indeed.

03:24.840 --> 03:28.430
All of the past highest-ranked chose those.

03:28.830 --> 03:31.030
No one yet has been able to read them,

03:31.030 --> 03:32.740
but they are said to be divine words.

03:33.460 --> 03:36.490
Supposedly, if you can 
read them, you will learn truth,

03:36.490 --> 03:38.480
and can have any wish come true.

03:38.760 --> 03:41.460
Each time the writing appears, it is different.

03:41.820 --> 03:44.200
What exactly might it be invoking?

03:44.470 --> 03:46.660
It piques one's curiosity, doesn't it?

03:47.100 --> 03:49.150
<i>If I can decipher this...</i>

03:50.700 --> 03:53.160
<i>I can return Ouken to the way he was.</i>

04:03.030 --> 04:03.920
Heh.

04:03.920 --> 04:07.400
Ridiculous. These are cursed.

04:07.640 --> 04:11.670
They thirst for much blood. 
I'm not interested.

04:15.210 --> 04:19.490
<i>Could he be the one to unravel the 
mystery of the Ranking of Kings?</i>

04:19.490 --> 04:22.170
Hmph! Is this all you've got?

04:23.450 --> 04:25.930
Come further inside.

04:25.930 --> 04:30.020
I am certain, King Desha, 
that your wish will be fulfilled.

04:37.360 --> 04:40.960
What became of the swords you 
gave to the kings before me?

04:41.420 --> 04:45.410
They started decaying as soon as they 
came in contact with the outside air.

04:45.410 --> 04:47.720
So, to prevent that from happening...

04:48.270 --> 04:52.030
...they had to constantly 
be bathed in blood, right?

04:52.030 --> 04:53.630
Why have such a thing?

04:54.210 --> 04:57.020
To kill multitudes of people, of course.

04:57.660 --> 05:00.380
We are continuously being manipulated.

05:16.910 --> 05:18.050
Who's this?

05:19.030 --> 05:21.830
Who knows? They have been 
here since long ago.

05:39.260 --> 05:40.810
What is this place?

05:41.640 --> 05:42.760
Is that a barrier?

05:43.090 --> 05:44.570
They are cells.

05:44.570 --> 05:45.590
It's what?

05:50.840 --> 05:52.600
A demon?

05:53.650 --> 05:55.630
This way, King Desha.

06:00.020 --> 06:01.130
Why, you...!

06:02.010 --> 06:04.560
Granting someone's wish—

06:04.560 --> 06:06.760
that is the role of these gods.

06:07.310 --> 06:09.960
Gods have a number of different roles.

06:09.960 --> 06:13.960
For some, their role is simply 
to die when the time comes.

06:15.240 --> 06:18.060
Your wish shall be granted.

06:18.530 --> 06:21.520
This little one will lose 
her girlish form, however.

06:25.790 --> 06:28.000
Oh, you wish to bow out?

06:28.760 --> 06:30.750
No, I'm dismissing my men.

06:35.410 --> 06:38.360
Apparently, Ouken's head is in this lake.

06:39.760 --> 06:41.460
What should we do now?

06:41.460 --> 06:42.360
Whoa...

06:43.360 --> 06:44.740
<i>Despa...</i>

06:44.740 --> 06:45.890
Brother?

06:45.890 --> 06:48.670
<i>I'm about to make Ouken human again.</i>

06:48.670 --> 06:49.830
Huh? How?

06:50.350 --> 06:52.260
I'm in the treasure vault right now.

06:52.860 --> 06:54.930
<i>You mean the divine one?</i>

06:54.930 --> 06:55.810
That's right.

06:56.550 --> 06:58.100
<i>I'd like to see that...</i>

06:58.500 --> 07:00.740
<i>The Divine Treasure Vault!</i>

07:02.110 --> 07:05.710
Oh, you can't! If you change 
him back now, he'll die!

07:05.710 --> 07:07.030
<i>What do you mean?</i>

07:07.450 --> 07:09.690
At the moment, he doesn't have his head.

07:11.040 --> 07:13.930
<i>Is this a sign that I should reconsider?</i>

07:15.060 --> 07:17.750
<i>Is it, Ouken?</i>

07:20.010 --> 07:23.340
<i>It's all right. We will have 
his head back shortly.</i>

07:25.080 --> 07:26.300
Very well.

07:26.300 --> 07:27.290
<i>Hurry.</i>

07:27.290 --> 07:27.880
Right.

07:28.260 --> 07:29.250
Captain!

07:29.600 --> 07:31.600
Let Ouken go on ahead into the lake.

07:31.600 --> 07:32.660
But sir...

07:32.660 --> 07:34.690
We just need to get his head back.

07:34.690 --> 07:37.350
Brother will deal with matters from there.

07:37.350 --> 07:38.110
All right.

07:46.400 --> 07:48.140
Just how far down is he—

07:50.020 --> 07:51.170
What's the matter?

07:51.550 --> 07:53.330
There's something pulling on him!

07:53.330 --> 07:54.660
Hurry and pull him back up!

07:54.660 --> 07:55.120
Right!

08:01.490 --> 08:02.880
This is bad!

08:06.740 --> 08:08.130
This is really bad.

08:09.390 --> 08:10.530
Prince Despa!

08:23.930 --> 08:26.080
Ouken! Your head!

08:27.170 --> 08:29.610
<i>Brother, we are ready here!</i>

08:31.400 --> 08:32.480
Forgive me.

08:32.880 --> 08:35.190
Ishihoga kinotana.

08:36.120 --> 08:38.150
Are you certain about this?

08:39.630 --> 08:42.120
Yeah. I'd give anything for this.

09:06.360 --> 09:07.710
Commander!

09:26.250 --> 09:27.480
Prince Despa...

09:28.650 --> 09:30.770
When Ouken became immortal,

09:30.770 --> 09:33.620
he could consume that which was 
rotten like it was nothing.

09:34.140 --> 09:37.370
That was because he didn't have 
to worry about getting sick.

09:37.370 --> 09:39.840
However, for a normal person...

09:40.870 --> 09:43.980
It's true! He has become human again!

09:47.570 --> 09:48.570
Ouken!

09:56.970 --> 09:59.750
Despa? Captain?

10:08.000 --> 10:11.100
I, Ouken, have returned!

10:11.100 --> 10:14.280
Mm-hmm. Welcome back, Ouken.

10:14.280 --> 10:16.710
Welcome back, Commander!

10:17.050 --> 10:19.680
Captain, is everyone doing well?

10:19.680 --> 10:23.000
Yes! They're all waiting 
for you to come back!

10:27.020 --> 10:30.050
What... evil deeds I've done...

10:31.510 --> 10:32.650
Ouken,

10:33.170 --> 10:37.340
the real you hasn't done a single bad thing.

10:38.080 --> 10:39.310
Despa...

10:41.010 --> 10:41.890
But then...

10:42.360 --> 10:45.580
your work with the sword has 
not been a pretty sight!

10:45.580 --> 10:50.000
You just rampaged about, and didn't 
do a single thing I taught you!

10:50.260 --> 10:51.410
Despa...

10:53.740 --> 10:58.500
It isn't funny! As your teacher, I have 
completely lost face! If I'm lucky...

10:58.500 --> 11:00.430
Prince Despa, now isn't the time.

11:02.350 --> 11:04.820
I'm obviously putting on an act!

11:06.660 --> 11:07.660
Ouken...

11:08.090 --> 11:08.900
Yes?

11:09.380 --> 11:11.920
It was Brother who saved you.

11:14.430 --> 11:17.870
Indeed, Brother is the one 
to become king of the world.

11:17.870 --> 11:19.190
He's the one who...

11:22.520 --> 11:25.830
<i>I wonder how that old sourpuss 
will react to this.</i>

11:25.830 --> 11:29.210
<i>Is he going to dance a jig? I can't wait!</i>

11:31.560 --> 11:33.610
Brother... Brother...

11:34.510 --> 11:35.490
Brother!

11:43.330 --> 11:44.430
What is this?

11:46.740 --> 11:50.910
What's going on here? Brother? Brother!

11:52.420 --> 11:54.470
Despa, what's the matter?

11:54.470 --> 11:58.200
I can't get through. This has
 never happened before.

11:59.940 --> 12:04.610
Brother, go claim the highest ranking 
and get us lots of treasures.

12:04.610 --> 12:05.600
Nonsense.

12:05.600 --> 12:07.240
How so?

12:07.240 --> 12:11.570
You know what happens to kings who 
become consumed with greed, right?

12:12.380 --> 12:16.510
Mm-hmm, but I'm sure 
you'll be fine, Brother.

12:23.000 --> 12:24.260
I bring news!

12:24.260 --> 12:28.280
King Desha has gone missing after 
entering the Divine Treasure Vault!

12:29.630 --> 12:31.250
Where is the treasure vault located?

12:31.250 --> 12:32.890
P-Prince Ouken!

12:34.600 --> 12:36.600
I will take you there.

12:37.170 --> 12:39.290
I'm going to go get Brother back.

12:44.040 --> 12:46.590
Very well. I'll leave you to it.

12:48.690 --> 12:51.520
Prince Despa, are you sure about this?

12:51.520 --> 12:56.300
Do you have any idea of the 
hell that man has returned from?

12:56.660 --> 12:58.730
There is nothing to worry about.

13:01.830 --> 13:03.000
Wait here.

13:03.000 --> 13:04.030
Yes, sir!

13:09.420 --> 13:11.520
I am Desha's younger brother, Ouken.

13:11.870 --> 13:13.920
I am here to make sure he is safe.

13:14.500 --> 13:16.100
I need you to let me inside.

13:19.640 --> 13:20.750
Then what?

13:21.310 --> 13:25.300
He went away. There was no longer any 
vestige of the king he was left.

13:25.630 --> 13:26.800
I see.

13:28.510 --> 13:29.620
What is it?

13:29.620 --> 13:31.590
We have an intruder.

13:31.590 --> 13:33.040
Have they been dispatched?

13:33.380 --> 13:35.620
Even a god would have his hands 
full with the gatekeepers.

13:45.760 --> 13:48.350
Are you trapped inside there?

13:53.890 --> 13:55.070
Is that so?

14:01.420 --> 14:02.980
Is there something I can help you with?

14:03.270 --> 14:05.010
Where is my brother?

14:05.010 --> 14:07.800
If you mean King Desha, 
he has already left.

14:07.800 --> 14:08.940
What the hell did you do?!

14:09.310 --> 14:11.590
We have not done anything.

14:13.050 --> 14:14.500
Stand aside.

14:14.500 --> 14:16.280
What do you intend to do?

14:16.280 --> 14:17.870
Stand aside, or I'll cut you down!

14:20.880 --> 14:23.350
It's all right. Let him pass.

14:26.660 --> 14:28.190
This way, please.

14:32.460 --> 14:35.560
Prince Ouken, we are not your foe.

14:35.990 --> 14:37.700
I will be the judge of that.

14:48.400 --> 14:49.760
You...

14:59.720 --> 15:02.910
I apologize for my treatment 
of the golems outside.

15:02.910 --> 15:06.550
It's all right. They will return 
to the way they were before long.

15:14.170 --> 15:17.560
<i>The Ranking of Kings... Kings...</i>

15:18.560 --> 15:19.700
<i>Can it be...</i>

15:33.590 --> 15:34.770
Listen to me, Ouken.

15:35.000 --> 15:37.620
If you ever find yourself facing
 a god, run away.

15:38.370 --> 15:42.000
They are enigmatic, and none 
can stand against them.

15:43.100 --> 15:46.860
Are you the one who did this?
 Impressive work.

15:51.830 --> 15:54.550
I never did like these golems much.

15:55.540 --> 15:58.260
Did you kill those who were inside?

15:59.140 --> 16:02.360
Hmm? Oh, so you didn't?

16:05.790 --> 16:08.630
Well, then, I'll do it.

16:08.630 --> 16:10.240
<i>On the other hand, Ouken...</i>

16:11.270 --> 16:15.860
<i>if you must confront one of 
them to protect someone,</i>

16:15.860 --> 16:17.980
<i>there is only one course 
of action to take—</i>

16:18.780 --> 16:19.720
Wait.

16:20.920 --> 16:22.160
Wait?

16:53.970 --> 16:57.210
How unsightly all of you are.

16:58.240 --> 16:59.630
You should all die!

17:07.710 --> 17:10.590
It can't be! It can't be! It can't be!

17:16.910 --> 17:20.980
<i>Misrepresent yourself, throw the 
god entirely off his guard,</i>

17:20.980 --> 17:24.850
<i>and make sure to finish him off 
before he really means business.</i>

17:25.290 --> 17:27.140
Never let your guard down.

17:39.390 --> 17:41.850
That's... Brother's!

17:45.590 --> 17:47.590
Brother!

17:51.610 --> 17:52.630
Brother...

18:07.090 --> 18:08.340
Commander!

18:09.000 --> 18:10.360
Stop me!

18:10.570 --> 18:11.690
Scrumdown!

18:17.010 --> 18:19.220
Commander, that wouldn't be...

18:19.660 --> 18:24.990
The price Brother paid to save me...
 was to lose his memories.

18:25.260 --> 18:26.510
That can't be!

18:26.510 --> 18:27.940
Then King Desha is...

18:28.750 --> 18:30.730
He must still be around here somewhere!

18:31.150 --> 18:32.920
We're taking him home, no matter what!

18:38.130 --> 18:41.220
<b>Ranking of Kings Low-Ranked Country
Kuhya Kingdom</b>

18:42.090 --> 18:44.700
Oof. Here we are.

18:48.720 --> 18:50.590
Bojji! Bojji!

18:50.970 --> 18:53.850
You can't go around flashing that 
much money in front of others!

18:55.230 --> 18:59.070
All of them live their lives working 
as hard as they can to make money.

18:59.070 --> 19:03.330
I ask that you refrain from doing anything 
to make them succumb to temptation.

19:05.810 --> 19:07.730
As long as you've learned your lesson.

19:09.970 --> 19:12.380
Mister, sorry to put you out.

19:12.380 --> 19:14.090
No trouble at all.

19:14.090 --> 19:17.410
No, I won't hear of it. Thanks.

19:17.680 --> 19:19.420
All right, let's go.

19:32.510 --> 19:35.520
Excuse me! We need a room!

19:35.760 --> 19:37.270
Sure!

19:37.680 --> 19:39.980
Oh, you're just children!

19:39.980 --> 19:42.240
We've got money, though. See?

19:44.200 --> 19:47.050
Oh, you do? This way, then.

19:47.050 --> 19:50.150
Hmm? In this case, it's all right.

19:53.090 --> 19:57.500
Now, then, it's going to worry me as 
long as you're carrying the money,

19:57.500 --> 19:59.080
so I'll hold on to it.

20:00.870 --> 20:05.180
Hey, Bojji, you can't go 
trusting people so readily.

20:06.720 --> 20:10.860
<i>Then again, that's one of the 
reasons why I came to like Bojji.</i>

20:11.110 --> 20:14.790
<i>Is it fair for me to tell 
Bojji not to trust others?</i>

20:14.790 --> 20:16.090
<i>On the other hand...</i>

20:28.580 --> 20:31.450
<i>Oh! I guess if I'm always there 
at his side, then it's okay.</i>

20:31.840 --> 20:35.840
<i>Yeah. As long as I'm by his 
side looking out for him...</i>

20:36.300 --> 20:36.950
Bojji!

20:48.600 --> 20:51.160
<i>You just keep being who you are.</i>

20:54.640 --> 20:56.950
<i>Mm-hmm, that's what's best.</i>

20:57.350 --> 20:58.790
Bojji!

21:19.870 --> 21:31.770
<i>Your precious words are now 
fluttering through the sky</i>

21:35.060 --> 21:40.770
<i>The nights when I was alone 
still had countless stars</i>

21:40.770 --> 21:45.900
<i>Even now, they're close at 
hand whenever I close my eyes</i>

21:46.410 --> 21:49.410
<i>With no destination, I kept on walking</i>

21:49.410 --> 21:52.240
<i>Although I was tired, I kept on walking</i>

21:52.240 --> 21:57.920
<i>I just wanted to remain in prayers forever</i>

21:57.920 --> 22:00.840
<i>Covered in scars, covered in mud</i>

22:00.840 --> 22:03.630
<i>stretching out hands that won't reach</i>

22:03.630 --> 22:13.430
<i>I want to seize a fragment of my 
hopes and dreams right this minute</i>

22:13.850 --> 22:19.610
<i>Keep smiling, keep smiling, 
you don't have to be strong</i>

22:19.610 --> 22:27.030
<i>That sweet smile, that 
sweet smile is all you need</i>

22:27.030 --> 22:31.620
<i>Your unique smile brings 
the power and strength</i>

22:31.620 --> 22:38.080
<i>to chase away all the clouds</i>

22:38.080 --> 22:48.430
<i>Your precious words are now 
fluttering through the sky</i>
